List this worktree's host routes, one per line: the name, the URL it answers on,
and the 127.0.0.1 port it targets. Needs a registered worktree: run `treerig up`
first. With --json, an array of {name, url, port}, plus subdomain and path when
the route has them.

Usage:
  treerig route ls [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for ls
      --json   machine-readable output

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -V, --version         output the version number
